.0,"cache_write_tokens":878.2857142857143,"input_tokens":2279.5714285714284,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":139.85714285714286,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":95512.0,"cache_write_tokens":35023.0,"input_tokens":130543.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":3374.0,"requests":4}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the `prog` string decision: specify whether `jira_onboard()` sets prog dynamically per entrypoint (`rebar bridge setup` vs legacy `rebar jira-onboard`) or leaves it fixed, and add an AC asserting `bridge setup --help` shows the primary spelling.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7","T9"],"criteria":["COH","E6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Main body: 'its argparse `prog=\"rebar jira-onboard\"` — the `prog` string is user-facing in `--help`'","Binding remediation: 'setup ... delegates those remaining arguments to `_jira_onboard.jira_onboard`. The wizard therefore continues to own all of its options, validation, interactive flow, and `--help`'","Binding remediation: 'The legacy top-level `jira-onboard` intercept remains and delegates to the same wizard.'"],"finding":"The main-body consumer list says the wizard's argparse `prog=\"rebar jira-onboard\"` is user-facing in `--help` and must migrate, but the binding-remediation section makes `bridge setup` a pass-through child that delegates to the SAME `_jira_onboard.jira_onboard` while ALSO keeping the legacy top-level `jira-onboard` intercept routed to that same function. A single `prog` string cannot correctly reflect both the `rebar bridge setup` and the legacy `rebar jira-onboard` invocation names; the plan does not state which prog string the shared wizard presents under each entrypoint.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f76d2990ee3f3ff83","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Enumerated consumers — jira-onboard' (`prog=\"rebar jira-onboard\"`) vs 'bridge setup dispatch shape' binding-remediation section","norm_id":"nd846324ae546728d","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A user runs `rebar bridge setup --help` and sees usage lines beginning `rebar jira-onboard`, contradicting the 'new spellings are primary' AC","The executor cannot tell whether to parameterize prog per-entrypoint or leave it stale"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that `jira_onboard()` accepts/derives its `prog` from the invoking entrypoint so `bridge setup --help` renders `rebar bridge setup` while the legacy intercept renders `rebar jira-onboard`, and add a parity assertion for the `--help` usage line under both names.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P4"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["45 file-impact entries (> 30)"],"finding":"Oversize signals suggest this unit may be too large for one session.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb59727dfac76fbbf","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"nd8e22e5830cb74a7","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split into smaller child tickets, each a coherent single outcome.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the enumerated bridge-probe dispatch-arm citation from '393-394' to the actual location `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:406-407` (the `if sub == \"bridge-probe\": return _bridge_probe(rest)` arm; 393-394 is the unrelated check-ac gate).","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the dispatch arm at 393-394'","src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:392-393 is `if sub == \"check-ac\": return gates.check_ac_cli(rest, tracker)`","search_files: bridge-probe dispatch is at src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:406 `if sub == \"bridge-probe\":` / :407 `return _bridge_probe(rest)`"],"finding":"The plan cites the bridge-probe CLI dispatch arm at 'the dispatch arm at 393-394', but lines 393-394 of src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py are the `check-ac` gate arm (`return gates.check_ac_cli(rest, tracker)`). The actual `bridge-probe` dispatch arm is at 406-407 (`if sub == \"bridge-probe\": return _bridge_probe(rest)`). The substantive premise (a dispatch arm routing to `_bridge_probe` exists) is verified; only the enumerated line location is inaccurate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff4cad0b18c1e8d4a","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Enumerated consumers — bridge-probe -> bridge check-access'","norm_id":"n9360b23b2657d1c7","priority":0.385,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","scenarios":["An implementer follows the cited 393-394 range and edits the wrong (check-ac gate) arm while migrating the bridge-probe consumer"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Change 'the dispatch arm at 393-394' to 'the dispatch arm at 406-407'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the enumerated `bridge-fsck` CLI dispatch patch site from '~309' to the real `bridge_fsck.main(rest)` arm at `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:264` inside `_dispatch_bridge` (255-264); line 309 is `compact_all_cli` and unrelated.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'CLI: `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py` (`_BRIDGE` frozenset ~121, dispatch arm ~309)'","Actual: `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:264: return bridge_fsck.main(rest)` inside `_dispatch_bridge` (arm at 255-264)","Actual line 309: `return _compact.compact_all_cli(rest)` — an unrelated command"],"finding":"For the `bridge-fsck` -> `bridge fsck` rename the plan enumerates the CLI dispatch patch site as `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py` '(`_BRIDGE` frozenset ~121, dispatch arm ~309)', but the actual dispatch arm that invokes `bridge_fsck.main(rest)` is at line 264 inside `_dispatch_bridge` (the bridge routing at 255-264). Line 309 is the unrelated `_compact.compact_all_cli` arm. The cited patch site for the `bridge_fsck.main` call is misplaced by ~45 lines onto a different function.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd780ff7bf4f3a29c","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Enumerated consumers — `bridge-fsck` -> `bridge fsck`: CLI: `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py` (`_BRIDGE` frozenset ~121, dispatch arm ~309)","norm_id":"ne3b9713fd9a11fff","priority":0.385,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","scenarios":["The implementer patches the compact dispatch arm (~309) instead of the real `bridge_fsck.main` routing at 264, leaving the `bridge fsck` compat routing unwired or editing the wrong arm."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Change 'dispatch arm ~309' to 'the `_dispatch_bridge` arm at ~255-264 calling `bridge_fsck.main(rest)`'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_ar